# Build output. Every Dockerfile that builds from the repository root
# (examples/deploy-agent, itk/Dockerfile.rust-agent, itk/Dockerfile.tck)
# copies the source and compiles inside the image, so a host `target/` is
# never needed there — it only made the build context gigabytes larger and,
# for the musl images, carried glibc artifacts in. `**/` also covers the
# per-agent directories under benches/sdk-comparison/harness.
**/target
